Previous research has shown that administration of the partial NMDA agonist D-cycloserine (DCS) before the 
reactivation  session  can  allow  destabilization  of  otherwise  insusceptible  fear  memories  (Bustos  et  al.,  2010; 
Espejo et al., 2016; Espejo et al., 2017; Gazarini, Stern, Piornedo, Takahashi, & Bertoglio, 2015; Ortiz et al., 2015).
